# GitHub reads this file for the "Cite this repository" button. It is the same
# reference as inst/CITATION, which is what citation("dfmtools") reads inside R;
# a change to either belongs in both. The deposit metadata Zenodo reads when a
# release is archived lives separately, in .zenodo.json.
#
# `version` and `date-released` track DESCRIPTION and are bumped with it. Once
# the first release is archived, add the Zenodo concept DOI -- the one that
# always resolves to the newest version -- as
#
#   identifiers:
#     - type: doi
#       value: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
#       description: "Concept DOI: resolves to the latest release."
#
# and mirror it into inst/CITATION and the README badge. .github/CONTRIBUTING.md
# has the whole release procedure.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use dfmtools in publications, please cite it as below."
title: "dfmtools: Bayesian Inference of Dynamic Factor Models"
abstract: >-
  Assists in the set-up of algorithms for Bayesian inference of dynamic factor
  models and factor augmented vector autoregressive models. Functions for
  posterior simulation and forecasting are largely based on
  the introductory texts of Chan, Koop, Poirier and Tobias (2019) and Luetkepohl
  (2006).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Franz X."
    family-names: Mohr
    email: franz.x.mohr@outlook.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8890-7781"
repository-code: "https://github.com/franzmohr/dfmtools"
url: "https://github.com/franzmohr/dfmtools"
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-13"
keywords:
  - r
  - bayesian-inference
  - dynamic-factor-models
  - time-series
  - econometrics
